WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.840
A short French prompt.

2
00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:05.850
Your town has decided to
close «la piscine municipale».

3
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.080
In its place: «un parking».

4
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.880
Underneath, three options:
«Article de blog»,

5
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.050
«Lettre formelle», «Page
de journal intime».

6
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:15.340
You choose one.

7
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.990
The prompt never names the one that fits.

8
00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:21.210
So how can a few lines of
French tell you the format,

9
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.900
the tone, and even what to say?

10
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:27.320
In this mission, you'll decode a
prompt with highlighter colours,

11
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.730
line by line.

12
00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:31.040
Then you'll take apart a model text,

13
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.520
from its title to its last line.

14
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.150
Your mission: find out
what a prompt is really

15
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.190
asking before you write a word.
